# Line endings are a build input, not a checkout preference.
#
# The repository stores LF and the published artifacts contain LF. What was missing
# was anything that made the *working tree* agree with them: with `core.autocrlf=true`
# and no attributes file, checkout wrote CRLF, and `python -m build` copied the working
# tree into the sdist. Measured before this file existed: 125 of 138 sdist members
# contained CRLF, against 0 in the published artifact. Nothing was broken by a mistake;
# the two builds simply read different bytes.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text, so a binary added later is left alone.
# `eol=lf` fixes the form written on checkout, which is what a build packages.
* text=auto eol=lf
